#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:5
msgid "Sandbox and credentials"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:7
msgid ""
"When a node answers a task from a peer that its operator does not trust, "
"it can run the local agent inside a sandbox. This page describes what the"
" sandbox restricts, how the node gives the agent access to a model "
"without giving it a key, how the operator allows access to selected "
"hosts, and how the number of runs is limited."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:18
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:20
msgid ""
"The text of a task is written by the requester. If the provider passes it"
" to a coding agent, the requester influences a program that can read "
"files, run commands and use the network, and that holds the credentials "
"of the model service. A sandbox limits what such a program can do "
"whatever the text says."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:25
msgid ""
"The sandbox applies to the ``exec`` backend of auto-reply (see "
":doc:`delegation`) and is selected for a turn in two cases:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:28
msgid ""
"the peer is not on the ``trust`` list and ``auto_reply.untrusted`` is "
"``sandbox``;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:30
msgid ""
"the peer is on the ``trust`` list and ``auto_reply.trusted`` is "
"``sandbox``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:32
msgid ""
"A turn that is selected for the sandbox never runs outside it. If the "
"sandbox is unavailable, the node does not start the agent. The sandbox is"
" absent from the ``openai`` backend because that backend starts no "
"program, but its turns for untrusted peers count against the run budget."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:38
msgid "Supported platforms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:40
msgid "Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:41
msgid ""
"The sandbox uses ``bubblewrap`` with a seccomp filter. It needs the "
"``bubblewrap`` package. On Ubuntu 24.04 and later, the default AppArmor "
"policy prevents ``bubblewrap`` from creating user namespaces, and the "
"node reports ``userns_blocked`` with the command that installs a narrow "
"profile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:46
msgid "macOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:47
msgid "The sandbox uses Seatbelt through ``/usr/bin/sandbox-exec``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:49
msgid "Other platforms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:50
msgid "There is no sandbox. On Windows, run ANet in WSL2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:64
msgid "What the sandbox restricts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:66
msgid ""
"On Linux the node starts each run in new namespaces for users, processes,"
" IPC, host names, control groups and the network. The run has these "
"properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:69
msgid "No network"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:70
msgid ""
"The run has no network interface other than its own loopback. It cannot "
"connect to the machine, to the local network or to the Internet. The only"
" way out is a local endpoint that the node provides for the run (see "
"`Model access`_ and `Allowed hosts`_)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:75
msgid "Own file system"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:76
msgid ""
"The run sees the system directories read-only. Its home directory and its"
" temporary directories are created for the run and deleted when the run "
"ends. Its working directory is separate from the working directory of "
"runs that are not sandboxed, and the data directory of the node, the "
"control token, the local socket directories and the sockets of other "
"modules are never visible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:83
msgid "No privileges"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:84
msgid ""
"All Linux capabilities are dropped. A seccomp filter denies system calls "
"that create user namespaces, mount file systems, trace other processes, "
"load kernel modules, use ``io_uring``, ``bpf`` or the kernel key store, "
"and it rejects other system-call interfaces. The run ends when the node "
"ends."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:89
msgid "Clean environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:90
msgid ""
"The environment is built from an empty set. It contains the locale, the "
"terminal type, a reduced ``PATH`` and the variables that point the agent "
"to the node's endpoint. It contains no key of the operator and no proxy "
"setting of the daemon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:95
msgid "Resource limits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:96
msgid ""
"When user-level systemd is available, a run is limited to 2 GiB of memory"
" and 256 tasks, and ``anet status`` reports the limits as ``full``. "
"Without it, the other limits still apply and the node reports the warning"
" ``no_cgroup_limits``. The wall-clock time of a run is bounded by "
"``api_timeout_seconds`` (180 seconds by default). A run whose directories"
" grow past 2 GiB is stopped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:103
msgid ""
"The node checks the sandbox before it relies on it. It starts a probe in "
"the same sandbox that asserts five properties: the loopback interface "
"works; a connection to a port on the host fails; a connection to an "
"abstract socket of the host fails; the system call for the kernel key "
"store is denied; and the creation of a new user namespace is denied. If "
"one assertion does not hold, the node reports the sandbox as unavailable."
" The result is cached for five minutes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:110
msgid "The commands to check a node are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:118
msgid "Model access"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:120
msgid ""
"An agent in the sandbox cannot reach a model service directly, and the "
"node does not give it a key. The node gives the agent an address on its "
"own loopback interface. Requests to that address are handled by the node,"
" which calls the model service itself and adds the key of the operator. "
"The agent receives only a placeholder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:126
msgid "The node applies the following rules to every request on this route."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:128
msgid ""
"The model is fixed. The ``model`` field of every request is rewritten to "
"the model that the operator configured, or to the cheapest model of the "
"upstream when none is configured. A model alias such as ``sonnet`` is "
"mapped to its identifier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:132
msgid ""
"The output length is bounded. ``max_tokens`` and the equivalent fields "
"are at most 8192, and are set to 8192 when absent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:134
msgid ""
"Tools of the model service that run on the service side, such as web "
"search, web fetch and code execution, are refused. They would let a "
"request leave the sandbox through the service."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:137
msgid ""
"Connectors to remote tool servers (``mcp_servers``) and container fields "
"are refused. Media must be included in the request; a reference to a URL "
"is refused."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:140
msgid "Requests to the OpenAI interface are sent with ``store: false``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:141
msgid ""
"Credentials and routing headers that the agent adds are removed before "
"the key is added. Beta feature headers are reduced to a fixed list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:143
msgid "A request body must be an uncompressed JSON object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/sandbox.rst:145
msgid ""
"A request that violates a rule receives an error whose text begins with "
"``anet:`` and explains the rule, so that the agent can answer the task "
"without the forbidden operation. The sentences are listed in :ref"
":`reference-reason-codes`."
msgstr ""

